## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, concrete incident response steps for a multi-tenant GCP SaaS, focusing on rapid containment, credential revocation, and rollback with auditable forensics.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation and containment
- Workload Identity and bindings management
- Network controls: NetworkPolicy, Private Service Connect, VPC Service Controls
- Forensics preservation and rollback playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: containment workflow
const onExfiltration = () => {
  isolateTenant();
  revokeIdentity();
  blockEgress();
  preserveForensics();
  runSyntheticTests();
  rollbackIfNeeded();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback playbook in CI/CD?
- What telemetry confirms containment success?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical tenant isolation at the messaging layer using Pub/Sub and IAM Conditions.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub isolation, IAM Conditions, per-tenant topics
- Dedicated service accounts per tenant
- Network controls to prevent egress
- CI validation with synthetic tenants

## Code Example
```javascript
// Binding example (pseudo)
{
  "bindings": [
    {
      "role": "roles/pubsub.publisher",
      "members": ["serviceAccount:tenant-sa@example.com"],
      "condition": {
        "title": "TenantTopicIsolation",
        "expression": "resource.name.startsWith(\"projects/PROJECT_ID/topics/tenant-\" + tenantId)"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
